  "provenance": "prospective",
  "question_text": "Top-band print-through: 6 wall loops against E-026's control",
  "hypothesis": "The ripples in the top band of every RIFT tile (photos IMG_1475, 1484, 1496, 1503; 4 Nov) are 15% grid infill printing through the face: the slice of the 10-inch baseline switches from solid to grid infill at 203.6 mm, where the cavity roof closes, and keeps grid about 0.8 mm behind the face's outer wall, under 3 walls, to 219.2 mm, the band's height in the photos. The dashes sit at that switch.",
  "prediction": "With 6 walls the grid sits about 2.6 mm behind the face and only from 209.6 mm (re-slice, 4 Nov), so this strip's face shows no stripes, or clearly fainter ones than E-026-A's. If it stripes as much as E-026-A, the cause is not infill behind the face; look next at the roof's solid-to-sparse switch and the outer-wall motion.",
  "why_this_test": "The one change that moves infill away from the face without touching the geometry; it adds about 13 min and 5.6 g to a full 10-inch tile.",
